# Lines the country test (country.bat) must write to COM1 with
# COUNTRY=081 (scripts/smoke-test): Japan, in its default code page, 932,
# with the year first. The currency is the yen sign, 5Ch in code page 932.
# COUNTRY.SYS has no Japan in code page 850, so CHCP 850 is refused.

^GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN$
^== COUNTRY$
^COUNTRY 081 DATE 2 TIME 1 CURRENCY "\\" FORMAT 0 DIGITS 0$
^SEPARATORS THOUSANDS "," DECIMAL "\." DATE "-" TIME ":" LIST ","$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 932 SYSTEM 437$
^Current date is \w{3} \d{4}-\d\d-\d\d$
^Enter new date \(yy-mm-dd\): $
^Current time is +\d+:\d\d:\d\d\.\d\d$
^NLSINFO  COM +544 \d\d-\d\d-\d\d +\d+:\d\d$
^== NLSFUNC$
^Active code page: 932$
^Invalid code page$
^Active code page: 932$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 932 SYSTEM 437$
^GRDOS-TEST-END$
